# FosOS base desktop. Development tools deliberately remain optional.
# The desktop session is FosOS Desktop (fosos-desktop .deb). No XFCE session.

# Display manager and X
# APT recommends are disabled, so packages that live-config and LightDM only
# recommend have to be listed here. user-setup creates the live account at
# boot; without it autologin has nobody to sign in and "user" / "live" is
# rejected. Xorg is required for the desktop. On Hyper-V prefer hyperv_drm
# (modesetting); fbdev remains a fallback if only /dev/fb0 appears.
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter
gir1.2-lightdm-1
user-setup
xserver-xorg
xserver-xorg-video-fbdev
xserver-xorg-input-libinput
xserver-xorg-input-all
xfonts-base
x11-xkb-utils
x11-xserver-utils
# Hyper-V guest tools (mouse/timesync/VSS); safe no-op on bare metal.
hyperv-daemons

# Web and connectivity
firefox-esr
network-manager
network-manager-gnome
wpasupplicant
ca-certificates
curl

# Audio, Bluetooth and common desktop integration
pipewire-audio
wireplumber
pavucontrol
blueman
gvfs
gvfs-backends
polkitd
# Debian 13 removed policykit-1-gnome. Without an agent named here, APT
# satisfies polkit-1-auth-agent with ukui-polkit, which pulls in OpenCV.
# fosos-session and fosos-theme start lxpolkit for FosOS.
lxpolkit
# APT recommends are off: without these, Intel SOF / SST laptops only get
# PipeWire "Dummy Output" (no real ALSA card). ThinkPad Tiger Lake needs SOF.
firmware-sof-signed
firmware-intel-sound
alsa-ucm-conf

# Essential user and compatibility tools
sudo
# APT recommends are off: without locales, LANG=en_US.UTF-8 is unsettable and
# GTK apps warn "Locale not supported". Calamares localecfg also needs it.
locales
# Well-known home folders (Documents, Downloads, Pictures, …). FosOS session
# runs xdg-user-dirs-update on login; /etc/skel seeds them at user create.
xdg-user-dirs
xarchiver
firmware-linux
# Laptop Wi-Fi: free firmware-linux is not enough. Explicit non-free-firmware
# blobs (Intel/Realtek/Atheros/Broadcom/MediaTek/misc). live-build keeps
# --firmware-chroot false so these must be listed here.
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-mediatek
firmware-misc-nonfree
wireless-regdb
# Calamares formats the UEFI system partition with mkfs.fat (dosfstools).
dosfstools
# UEFI Secure Boot: Microsoft-trusted shim + Debian-signed GRUB. Kept in the
# squashfs so Calamares installs boot with Secure Boot on. Do not add grub-pc
# here (Conflicts with grub-efi-amd64); hybrid ISO BIOS bits are binary-stage.
shim-signed
grub-efi-amd64-signed
grub-efi-amd64
mokutil
efibootmgr
# Applies /etc/default/keyboard to the text consoles. Without it, a layout
# chosen in the installer (for example Croatian) never reaches Ctrl+Alt+F2.
console-setup
# initramfs prefers zstd when present; without it update-initramfs warns and
# falls back to gzip.
zstd
# bootappend-live uses splash → plymouth. APT recommends are off, so ship the
# label plugin and themes explicitly (avoids label-pango.so / themes warnings).
plymouth
plymouth-label
plymouth-themes

# Remote Desktop (RDP). Inbound Windows-like host via xrdp (separate session);
# outbound client via FreeRDP. Off until Settings → Remote Desktop enables it.
freerdp3-x11
xrdp
xorgxrdp
